      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "Additional evidence, still on a slime 0.3.0-based build (P6 B200, 10 steps each).\n\n**This change on four Qwen3.5 layouts.** The flag is set in `Attention.__init__`, and the probe only measures. Counts are summed over all ranks.\n\n| Layout | replicated params / flagged / differing across TP (step 10) |\n|---|---|\n| 35B-A3B TP2 PP1 EP8 SP | 300 / 300 / 0 |\n| 122B-A10B TP2 PP4 EP8 SP | 360 / 360 / 0 |\n| 122B-A10B TP4 PP4 EP8 SP | 2880 / 2880 / 0 |\n| 397B-A17B TP2 PP8 VPP2 EP8 SP | 3600 / 3600 / 0 |\n\n**Numerics, 35B-A3B.** Same seed and data: two runs with this change (F1, F2) and one without it (U).\n\n| pair | loss max / mean abs diff | grad_norm max / mean abs diff |\n|---|---|---|\n| F1 vs F2 (run-to-run noise) | 1.65e-3 / 7.5e-4 | 1.08 / 0.17 |\n| F1 vs U | 2.18e-3 / 4.5e-4 | 0.51 / 0.07 |\n| F2 vs U | 1.22e-3 / 6.0e-4 | 1.11 / 0.15 |\n\nWithout the change, 1656 of 2400 replicated rank-params differ across TP by step 10. With it, none do. Step time is unchanged (72.4 / 71.9 s vs 71.9 s).\n\n**CI.** The only failing check, `test_swe_workspace_diff.py::test_patch_uses_actual_image_baseline_without_changing_git_index[unstaged]`, looks like a flaky race in the test added in #2457. Git's background maintenance removed `.git/objects/maintenance.lock` during `copytree`. The test passes on `main` at the same commit and is unrelated to this change, which only touches `qwen3_5.py`. Could a maintainer re-run it?\n\nReady for review whenever someone has time.\n",
